==Strategy==
==='''Chapters 1 & 2'''===
Use three meatshields and Bahamut Cat to take out the Ursamajor, you can also use other cats with more than 350 range like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon]] or [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bath Cat]]. Long-range and anti-Aliens are useful as always against Ursamajor. Bring an anti-Red to handle the influx of One Horns. They reward you with a LOT of cash so going all out with cats isn't a bad idea.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The major difference for this stage is that [[Calamary]] appears as the boss instead of Ursamajor. The Cyberhorn, One Horn and other peons still appear as a constantly spawning threat but the weaken effect from Calamary is the real troublemaker here.

Calamary doesn't have too much health if you have all of Ch 1 & 2 treasures (as low as 135,000 hp and 3,600 attack power when you first encounter the stage) but she has a 50% chance to weaken all attacks by 90% with decent attack speed and from 500 range. Your cats will be doing 10% of their normal damage unless you bring Weaken Immune  cats or can perma-freeze Calamary.

The usual freeze-cheese for aliens doesn't really help much against Calamary because of the massive stack of One Horn and Cyberhorns that build up in front of her. However, the stack of rhinos also leads to massive income, ensuring that you can summon all your big units and max your Worker Cat if staggered properly. If you can freeze the rhinos then the match gets significantly easier as you'll lose less of your attacking force.

You'll want to stack up good anti-Red and anti-Alien units like [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], [[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|Momotaro]] or [[Voli (Uber Rare Cat)|Volta]] for freeze effects and strong units like [[Viking Cat (Rare Cat)|Thor Cat]] and [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat]]. Ranged cats like [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Legs]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]] do a great job of helping as do the Long-range ubers you may have access to.

Overall, as long as you can withstand the waves of rhinos you will eventually whittle down Calamary and end the fight.

